# psg_mod.checks - one row per CHECK of fixtures/src/psg_mod.s (D-125, plan 05-07; checks 4..8 from its Task 2). Columns separated by one TAB: check index (1-based), slug, class tag, meaning.
# The PSG is write only (H8-24): these checks judge the guest's own data with two in-guest computations each (GUEST); every judgement of the sound is the runner's, against fixtures/src/psg_mod.aexp (ER-21). A pass is not a support claim (ER-4).
id=28
checks=8
1	table-sum-2	GUEST:table-sum	Table 2 (select 2, mod_r7) summed by a table walk equals the sum of the counter 0..31 (496): the low bytes XOR and the high bytes XOR, ORed, are zero
2	table-sum-4	GUEST:table-sum	Table 4 (select 4, mod_noise4) summed by a table walk equals the sum of the counter 0..31 (496): the low bytes XOR and the high bytes XOR, ORed, are zero
3	table-sum-5	GUEST:table-sum	Table 5 (select 5, mod_noise5) summed by a table walk equals the sum of the counter 0..31 (496): the low bytes XOR and the high bytes XOR, ORed, are zero
4	table-sum-3	GUEST:table-sum	Table 3 (T2, select 2, mod_dda) summed by a table walk equals the sum of the counter 0..31 (496): the low bytes XOR and the high bytes XOR, ORed, are zero
5	dda-runs	GUEST:dda-schedule	The timer handler ran once per value of dda_list: its run count equals the length of the list counted by a walk to its end mark (9)
6	dda-writes	GUEST:dda-schedule	The handler made one R6 write per value of dda_list: its write index equals the same length (9)
7	dda-sum	GUEST:dda-schedule	The handler's running sum of the values it wrote equals the sum of dda_list by a backward walk in the main loop (5 + 5 + 20 + 3 + 31 + 0 + 12 + 12 + 27 = 115)
8	dda-order	GUEST:dda-schedule	The handler's log of the values written, in write order, equals dda_list walked forwards: the OR of the differences is zero
